  58:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        Stop 3 mode. Wake-up from Stop 3 mode could be following to an event or
  59:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        an interrupt according to low power mode intrinsic request called
  60:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        (__WFI() or __WFE()). (Regulator state on U5 devices is managed
  61:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        internally but regulator parameter is kept for product compatibility).
  62:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
  63:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWREx_EnterSHUTDOWNMode() function to enter the whole system in
  64:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        Shutdown mode. Wake-up from Shutdown mode can be following to an external
  65:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        reset (NRST pin), a WKUP pin event (configurable rising or falling edge),
  66:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        or an RTC event occurs (alarm, periodic wakeup, timestamp), or a tamper
  67:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****        detection.
  68:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
