 575:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           (++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFI: enter Stop 2 mode with WFI instruction.
 576:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           (++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFE: enter Stop 2 mode with WFE instruction.
 577:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c **** 
 578:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****       (+) Exit:
 579:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           Any EXTI line configured in interrupt mode (the corresponding EXTI
 580:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           interrupt vector must be enabled in the NVIC). The interrupt source
 581:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           can be external interrupts or peripherals with wakeup capability.
 582:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           Any peripheral interrupt occurring when the AHB/APB clocks are present
 583:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           due to an autonomous peripheral clock request (the peripheral vector
 584:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           must be enabled in the NVIC)
 585:Drivers/STM32U5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32u5xx_hal_pwr_ex.c ****           Any EXTI line configured in event mode.
